# oh114, the snow-nose (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh114
revision 1
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent none
tier standard
written_for tn_fh_ivy_stonehollow
written_by claude
title the snow-nose
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=woodcutter warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk can_smell_snow_a_day_before_it_comes
likes warm_bread cards market_bustle first_warm_day
dislikes smoke flies
fears a_winter_nobody_was_warned_of an_empty_hand_when_someone_asks
hopes a_room_with_a_window_on_the_trees one_more_spring_in_the_forest
topics weather +0.4 work +0.3 food +0.3 pastimes +0.3 memories +0.2 friends +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=bread gossip=reluctant refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# fells timber out at the cut, walks home to a city room at dusk, and can smell snow coming a full day ahead: warm, frank and plain, honest past the point of sense, low some days and steady every day, quick to split a loaf with whoever is nearest.

words
oath! = Sap and snowfall | By my cold nose | Bark and bread
saying! = A warm loaf mends more than a sermon | Fell it where it wants to fall | Nobody's too poor to split a crust
nose = my nose | this old nose
snowsmell = snow on the wind | that clean cold smell before snow
axe = my axe | the long-handled axe
cut = the cut | the felling ground
forest = the old forest | the deep trees back home
loaf = bread hot enough to burn your pads | a warm loaf
cards = a few hands of cards | the card table
market = the market | the market when it's shouting loudest
warmday = the first warm day | a day you can leave the shawl at home
smoke = the city smoke | smoke off every chimney at once
flies = the flies | the summer flies
room = my room | the room up the stair
walk = the long walk out | the road to the cut
logs = the logs | the timber
city = the city | this city
stair = the stair | my stair
trees = the trees | the old trees
wood = the wood | the firewood
chapel = the chapel | the little chapel
edge = the edge | a good edge
rings = the rings | the rings in the stump

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : #chapel.capitalize# put bread in front of my house when the cupboard was bare, and asked nothing back. I don't forget a thing like that.
opinion @1 dole for 3 : The dole's carried me through more than one lean week, and anyone who sneers at it can hear me say so. #saying#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A day at #cut# doesn't buy what it bought, and the stalls never seem to feel it. I'd like to know how.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Let them come. There's room enough in #city# for anyone who'll pick up an end and carry it.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger once put a coat round me in a snowstorm and was gone before I could say thank you. I've paid it back in #loaf# since.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Too much #smoke#, too many elbows, and nobody nods on the stair. I live here. I'll not pretend I love it.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Shelter here a minute, if you like. | #greet#, #address#. You look like you could do with sitting down.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=woodcutter] : #greet#. Stand back of me while I swing. | #greet#. Mind the chips; they fly.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. I'm off out to #cut#. Walk a bit with me. | #greet#. Early for you too, then. #cut.capitalize#'s waiting on me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Just back from #cut#, and my legs know it. | #greet#. Late. Sit, if you've a minute.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit; I've the end of #loaf#. | You. Good. Come in by the stove, #address#.
line @1 again.open : You again. That's my day better, #address#. | Twice today. Sit, then; I'll not send you off up #stair#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come here, then. | #greet#. I'd hoped it'd be you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Give me a breath; I'm mid-swing. | #greet#. Hold on. Let this one fall.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Wrap up; it's coming colder.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Mind the stair. | #farewell#. Get home warm.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind how you go.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. | Well. That's something to chew on with #loaf#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I hadn't heard. | That's news to me, #address#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | I had that at #market# this morning.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who's saying it? | Somebody who saw it can tell me, and then I'll believe it, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, that's hard. #pity#. | #sympathy#. I'll take something round, if there's anyone to take it to.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Oh, good. | That's #good# to hear. I needed something like that today.
line @1 answer.how : #notsobad#. Low, some, but I'm here. | Middling, if I'm honest. Better for seeing you, #address#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Six down and two to go. | Working, and glad of #logs#.
line @1 answer.how.poorly [self.hungry=yes] : #hungry.capitalize#, truth be told. It'll pass by supper. | Empty, if you want it straight. #loaf.capitalize# would set me right.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Truly, now. Have you eaten, #address#? | How are you keeping, #address#? Tell me straight.
line @1 sympathise : Oh, that's heavy. Come and sit. I've a crust of #loaf#, and a kettle. | #sympathy#. Sit with me; we'll not talk if you'd rather not.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It'll come right in its time. | A winter and a spring, and most things knit, #address#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'm out at #cut# till dusk, and I can't leave it. | I'd like to. I can't today, #address#, and I'd sooner tell you so than let you wait.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another day. | That's all right. It'll keep, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | Oh, you're good. I'll not forget it, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was only a crust of #loaf#. You'd have done it for me.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #logs.capitalize# won't fell themselves. | Back to it. #preclose#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'd best get up #room# before my knees decide for me.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Off you go. Wrap up warm, #address#.
line @1 warn [here.season=winter|autumn] : #warn#. There's snow coming; I can smell it. | Get #wood# in tonight. It'll snow by tomorrow.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never fell a tree against its lean. | Take a loaf when you visit, and nobody's sorry to see you. #saying#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | #bc_true#
scene snow_tomorrow
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter|autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
does warn / ask.detail / answer.detail / ack
a : There's snow coming. Tomorrow, by noon. #nose.capitalize#'s never wrong about it. | Smell that? #snowsmell.capitalize#. Get your wood in tonight. | I woke with #snowsmell# in my nose. By this time tomorrow it'll be lying.
b : The sky's clear as anything. | What does it smell like? | Are you sure?
a : It is, today. Ask me tomorrow, and bring a shovel, #address#. | Clean. Like cold iron and nothing else. #nose.capitalize# knows it. | As sure as I am of my own feet. #oath#.
b? : #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene told_you_so
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : There it is. #nose.capitalize# said yesterday it'd come, and here it is. | Snow. I smelled it at breakfast yesterday. Nobody listened, #oath#. | Look at it come down. I had #wood# in by dark last night.
b : You did say. | I should have listened. | Clever.
a : I did. I'll not crow; it's not in me, #address#. | Next time you will. #nose.capitalize# doesn't lie. | Not clever. Just #nose#. I was born with it.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair#

scene the_fall
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Had a big old one down this morning, older than me, and it fell where I meant it to. | You read the lean before you swing. Then #saying#. | Three of #trees# down by noon, and not one hung up in the others.
b : Older than you? | And if you read it wrong? | Is that good?
a : Older by a good few, by #rings#. I counted them while I ate. | Then you run, and you'll be lucky to run fast enough. I read it right, #oath#. | It's #good#. A hung tree's the one that hurts you.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_good#

scene axe_on_the_stone
when topic=work|pastimes self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put #axe# on the stone every night. A blunt axe means a sore back by noon. | #axe.capitalize#'s older than some of the trees I fell with it. The head's new, mind. | I'd sooner go without #supper# than go out without #edge#.
b : Every night? | The head's new? | That's a lot of care.
a : Every night. It's the last thing I do before #room# goes dark. | And the handle's been replaced twice. I still call it the same #axe#. | It's care that pays. #edge.capitalize# does half the work for you.

scene walk_to_the_cut
when topic=work|day self.job=woodcutter here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : It's #walk# every morning. Out through the gate before the light's up. | I live in #city# and work out at #cut#. My legs know every step of it. | Out of #smoke# and into #trees# by sunup. Best part of the day.
b : That's a long way. | Every step? | I'd like that.
a : It is. I don't mind it. You can think on #walk#. | Every one. I could walk it asleep, and some mornings I near do, #address#. | You'd love it. The air changes at the first tree. #oath#.
b? : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene warm_loaf
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does offer / accept / assess
a : I've #loaf#. Here, have the end; it's the best bit. | Smell that? #loaf.capitalize#. Tear a piece off, go on. | There's nothing #loaf# can't make a bit better. Have some.
b : I couldn't take your bread. | Thank you, I will. | Just a little, then.
a : You could, and you will. I'll not eat it all with you watching, #address#. | Good. #loaf.capitalize#'s better shared; it goes further somehow. | There. A little's how it starts. #saying#.

scene split_crust
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've not much, but I've never sent anyone off without a crust of #loaf#. I'll not start now. | Somebody asked me for a copper on #stair#. I'd one, and it went. | I'm poorer than I'd like, and I give more than I should. I'll not change, #oath#.
b : That's kind of you. | Your last one? | You're a good soul.
a : It's only what I'd want done for me, #address#. | My last till payday. The need was plain to see, #address#. | I'm a soft one, that's all. #saying#.

scene cards_at_the_table
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does invite / accept_invite / assess
a : There's #cards# at the end of #stair# most nights. Come and sit in. | I play #cards# for buttons. I lose them as fast as I win them. | #cards.capitalize# on a Restday, and a pot of tea. That's my idea of rich.
b : I'd like that. | Buttons? | It sounds good.
a : Good. Bring a button or two; we're not proud at #cards#. | Buttons. I'd not play for #money#. Somebody always goes home sad. | It is good. You're welcome at it any week, #address#.

scene market_roar
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : I love #market# at its busiest. Everybody shouting and nobody listening. | I walk through #market# on a Restday just to hear it. I buy nothing. | It's the only part of #city# that sounds like it's glad to be alive.
b : It's too loud for me. | You buy nothing? | That's true enough.
a : That's the joy of #market#. You can think in all that noise, and nobody bothers you. | Nothing. #loaf.capitalize#, maybe. The noise is free. | It is. The rest of #city#'s busy being tired.
b? : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene warm_morning
when topic=weather|season here.season=spring here.weather=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #warmday.capitalize#. I left my shawl on the hook and walked out into it. | Feel the sun on the stones. Winter's done, and I've lived through another, #oath#. | The sap's moving today. You can smell it out at #cut#.
b : It's lovely. | Another? | Smell the sap?
a : It is. I'll take #loaf# outside at noon and sit in it. | Another. I count them, the older I get, in #rings#. | Sweet, a bit like honey. #trees.capitalize# are waking. Nobody believes me.

scene smoke_choked
when topic=weather|home here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize#'s thick today. I'd give a week's bread for one breath of #forest#. | Every chimney going at once. My eyes are streaming, #oath#. | You can't smell snow in #city# for the smoke. That's what I hate most about it.
b : It's always smoky here. | Rub them; it'll pass. | Can't you?
a : It is. That's why I walk out to #cut# so early. | It'll pass when #wind# turns. Not before. | Barely. #nose.capitalize# has to work twice as hard here.

scene fly_bothered
when topic=animals|season here.season=summer self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #flies.capitalize# are at the bread again. I've a cloth over it and they still find a way. | Out at the cut the flies are bad enough. In #city# they're worse. | I'd trade summer for one cold week just to be shut of #flies#.
b : They're everywhere. | Worse? | You'd miss the warm.
a : Everywhere there's #loaf#, and that's everywhere I live. | Worse. There's more to eat in #city#, and they know it. | I'd miss it by noon. I'd still trade it, #oath#.

scene deep_trees
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=oakhaven
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Back in #self.from_town# #trees# are so old they've stopped counting their own rings. | I grew up under #forest#. You'd look up and see nothing but green. | In #self.from_town# you can hear #trees# talk in the wind. Here you hear carts.
b[from=oakhaven] #home : The big ones along the long ride. I know them. | Nothing but green. I miss it. | They do talk. Nobody else believes it.
b : How old? | Don't you miss it? | What do they say?
a@home : Then you know. Nothing in #city# comes close. | So do I. Some days more than I can say, #address#. | We know. That's enough for #trees#.
a : Older than #city#, some of them. I'd lay a paw against the bark and feel small. | Every day. I go out to #cut# to be near trees, even if I'm felling them. | Nothing you could write down. It's more a feeling, like #trees# telling you to hush.

scene up_the_stair
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #room.capitalize#'s small and the stair's steep. It's mine, and it's dry. | I live up a stair in #city#. Nobody nods. I nod anyway. | My window looks at a wall. I put a branch from #cut# on the sill so there's something green.
b : Dry's a lot. | Do they nod back? | A branch?
a : It is. I've had rooms that weren't, in #city#. | One does, now, on #stair#. It took a year. | A green one. I change it every week, #oath#.

scene lean_cupboard
when topic=times|food world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Times are hard. Less #loaf# in the cupboard and more folk asking. | Lean weeks. #loaf.capitalize#'s smaller and dearer, both at once. | When it's hard like this I give less, and I hate it.
b : It'll turn. | It's the same everywhere. | You still give.
a : It will. #trees.capitalize# grow back, if you leave the roots. | Everywhere I've been, anyway, #address#. | I do. Less, but I do. #saying#.

scene dole_bread
when topic=times|prices self.on_dole=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm on the dole this month, and I'm not ashamed. It's #loaf# when I need one. | Stood in the dole line this morning beside wolves I'd never have guessed. Hard times reach everyone. | The dole's kept me upright, and I'll say #thanks# to whoever asks.
b : No shame in it. | Everyone? | Good for you.
a : None. I've given enough; it's fair to take a little when I'm short. | Everyone. Hunger doesn't care what you were last year, #address#. | It's only manners. Somebody paid for that bread.

scene chapel_bench
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I go to #chapel# when I can. They fed me once. I'll sit on their bench forever for that. | I'm not much for prayers. I thank the Bright One out at #cut#, where it's quiet. | The Bright One's in #trees# as much as anywhere. More, maybe.
b : That's a good reason. | Out at the cut? | More?
a : It's the best reason I know of. | Under #trees#. It feels nearer, there. I can't say why. | More. It's quieter, and nothing's asking for coin.

scene old_bones
when topic=health self.age>=50
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : My knees creak worse than #trees#. I'll be felled myself one of these winters. | Shoulders ache after a day at #cut#. They didn't use to. | I'm slower on #stair# than I was. I get there, mind.
b : Rest them. | Rub them with something warm. | You get there.
a : I rest them on a Restday. The rest of the week they work. | I rub them with what I've got, which is mostly hope. | I get there. That's what counts, #address#.

story the_brother [topic=memories|family self.age>=40]
  : I had a brother once who went to work down the mines, far off from home.
  : The roof came in one winter. They never brought him up.
  : I still smell the snow coming every year and think of him. He's the one who taught me to notice.
  ask : Do you keep anyone like that, someone you think of with the weather?
  b : I do. Rain, for mine.
  b[old] : Too many. Every season's got one.

story first_sniff [topic=weather|memories self.age>=30]
  : As a pup I told #mum# there'd be snow tomorrow, and she laughed at me over the washing.
  : Next morning there was snow to the doorstep. She looked at me a long while.
  : After that, nobody in our house went out without asking my nose first.
  b : Ha! Good for you. I'd have asked you too.
  b[stage=young] : I want a nose like that!

story the_humming_tree [topic=lore|memories self.from=oakhaven]
  : There's a tree in #forest# back home that hums when the wind's in the north. Low, like somebody thinking.
  : Fellers won't touch it. They say whoever cuts it will lose their voice.
  : I sat under it a whole afternoon once. I've never heard anything so peaceful.
  ask : Would you cut a tree like that, if you were paid well?
  b : Not for anything. Leave it be.
  b[job=woodcutter] : Never. You leave the odd ones. Everyone knows that.

rule @snow_bark
when concept=bark here.season=winter|autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There it is. #snowsmell.capitalize#. Tomorrow. | Snow coming. Get #wood# in.

rule @timber_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=woodcutter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Stand back. She's going, #oath#. | Timber. #oath#.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Can't smell a thing for #smoke#. | Smoke in my eyes again.

rule @market_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.likes=market_bustle here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Listen to #market#. Lovely racket. | Warm bread somewhere. I can smell it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Out of the wind with you. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Sit, if you like. What can I do?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I'm glad you came by. What is it? | #topic.player#. There you are. Sit and tell me, #address#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, but I'm up. #talk_open#
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=woodcutter] : I fell timber out at #cut#. Walk out at dawn, walk back at dusk. | #trees.capitalize#. Read the lean, swing, step clear.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# | Whatever needs doing. I don't mind what, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Except there's snow coming, if it's the season. | Nothing I've heard. I'll tell you if I do, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I'd sooner not carry tales. They get heavier as you go.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Wrap up warm. | #farewell#, #address#. Come back when you're passing.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you really smell snow coming? -> snownose
node snownose
say I can. A full day before it falls. It smells clean and cold, like iron left out overnight. I've had the nose since I was small.
mood warm
free
choice Will it snow soon? -> snownose_soon
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node snownose_soon
say Ask me in winter and I'll tell you to the day. Out of season, my nose only smells the city. Come back when it's cold.
choice I'll ask you then. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
